# Optimize Rishta codebase: kill duplication, add shared OOP helpers

## Context

User asked for a ponytail-driven optimization pass across the whole codebase, using OOP concepts to write less code for the same behavior. Full read-through of all 22 files is done. The core layer (`api.dart`, `providers.dart`, `models.dart`, `widgets.dart`, `theme/`) is already well-factored — `RemoteRepo`, `RemoteAsync`, `Json`, `AsyncView` are reused properly. The wins live in the **feature screens**, where the same small patterns are re-implemented per-screen.

Decision already made: keep the hand-curated 65-country list in `auth_screen.dart` (no new dependency).

## Changes

### 1. `core/widgets.dart` — add `ProfileNameBadge`
Name + age + verification check, rendered identically in feed and matches:

- [feed_screen.dart:170-182](app/lib/features/feed/feed_screen.dart#L170-L182) — `Row[Flexible(Text('name, age')), VerificationBadge]` on a photo scrim (white text)
- [matches_screen.dart:54-65](app/lib/features/matches/matches_screen.dart#L54-L65) — same Row inside a ListTile title (theme-colored text)

```dart
/// One-line name + age + verified check. Reused by feed cards and match rows.
class ProfileNameBadge extends StatelessWidget {
  const ProfileNameBadge({super.key, required this.name, this.age,
      this.verification = VerificationStatus.pending, this.style});

  final String name;          // ProfileSummary.displayName
  final int? age;
  final VerificationStatus verification;
  final TextStyle? style;     // omit on photo scrims, theme style in list rows

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Row(
        mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
        children: [
          Flexible(
            child: Text(
              age == null ? name : '$name, $age',
              overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,
              style: style,
            ),
          ),
          if (verification.isVerified) ...[
            const SizedBox(width: 4),
            VerificationBadge(status: verification),
          ],
        ],
      );
}
```
The 4px gap + you get `'name, age'` in exactly one place. Both call sites collapse to ~3 lines.

### 2. `core/widgets.dart` — add `ErrorText`
The `Semantics(liveRegion) > Text(error)` block is pasted in four screens with an identical shape (error hardcoded to the theme error color in three of them):

- photos_screen.dart:106-111, profile_form_screen.dart:240-249, selfie_screen.dart:161-169, and auth_screen.dart's `_ErrorBanner` (banner variant, same intent)

```dart
/// Inline (non-banner) error text with live-region semantics — the error
/// message pattern every onboarding step repeats.
class ErrorText extends StatelessWidget {
  const ErrorText(this.message, {super.key});
  final String message;
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Semantics(
        liveRegion: true,
        child: Text(message, style: TextStyle(color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.error)),
      );
}
```

### 3. `core/widgets.dart` — add `FormProgress` mixin
The `_busy = true; _error = null; try { … } on catch { _error = messageFor(e); } finally { _busy = false; }` skeleton is handwritten in **four** stateful-consuming screens:

- profile_form_screen.dart `_save` (113-133)
- photos_screen.dart `_add` (35-54)
- selfie_screen.dart `_capture` (103-129)
- auth_screen.dart `_run` (153-163) — already extracted, but reimplemented differently

```dart
/// Wraps a Future in the busy/error lifecycle every onboarding step repeats.
/// Screen state merges `with FormProgress` and calls `_progress(fn)`.
mixin FormProgress<T extends StatefulWidget> on State<T> {
  bool _busy = false;
  String? _error;
  bool get busy => _busy;
  String? get error => _error;

  Future<void> _progress(Future<void> Function() fn) async {
    setState(() { _busy = true; _error = null; });
    try { await fn(); }
    catch (e) { if (mounted) setState(() => _error = messageFor(e)); }
    finally { if (mounted) setState(() => _busy = false); }
  }
}
```
Screens become `with FormProgress` and replace their bespoke try/catch with `_progress(() async { … })`, deleting `_busy`/`_error` fields. Auth's `_run` stays (it has Firebase-specific error mapping) but keeps the same shape.

### 4. Report reasons — one shared constant + one shared call
`['Inappropriate photos', 'Harassment', 'Fake profile', 'Spam or scam']` is hardcoded twice and the POST `/reports` block exists twice:

- feed_screen.dart:266 + 295-301 (`_blockSheet` reports or blocks, reasons + 'Other')
- matches_screen.dart:94-114 (`_report` dialog + POST with same 4 reasons + matchId)

Move to `core/api.dart` (alongside `Api`, both screens already own an `api` via providers):

```dart
/// Standard report reasons, shared by feed and match reporting.
const kReportReasons = ['Inappropriate photos', 'Harassment', 'Fake profile', 'Spam or scam'];
```
Feed's `_blockSheet` becomes `[...kReportReasons, 'Other']`. Matches calls the constant. Do **not** extract the shared `_postReport` helper on matches (it adds `matchId`); a constant is the lazy win here.

### 5. Dead code / stray widgets
- **chat_screen.dart:46** — `StreamChat(client: stream, child: …)` wraps the channel UI but nothing below calls `StreamChat.of(context)` (only `StreamChannel`/`StreamMessageListView`/`StreamMessageInput`, which read their own InheritedWidgets). Delete the wrapper, keep `MainStreamChat`-created client. Verify with `flutter analyze` — unused import falls out if wrong.
- **auth_screen.dart** — the file re-declares `_pink/_pinkDeep/_pinkLight/_tanBase/_tanDark/_tanCard` instead of using the existing `Tokens.pinkAccent/pinkLight/tanBase/tanDark` from [tokens.dart](app/lib/core/theme/tokens.dart). Add `tanCard` to `Tokens`, then inline-import `theme.dart` and delete the six consts. (VSCode lint already fired on the `theme.dart` import once — the file genuinely needs it now.)

### 6. No new dependencies, no new packages
Recap: country list stays as-is. Everything above uses only existing deps (flutter_riverpod, firebase, stream_chat) via existing shared files.

## Files touched

- `app/lib/core/widgets.dart` — add `ProfileNameBadge`, `ErrorText`, `FormProgress`
